==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|lothario}}

===Etymology===
Lothario, an unscrupulous seducer of women in ''The Impertinent Curious Man'', a [[Story within a story|metastory]] in ''[[Don Quixote]]''. Later, a seducer in the play ''{{w|The Fair Penitent}}'' (1703) by {{w|Nicholas Rowe (writer)|Nicholas Rowe}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A man whose chief [[interest]] is [[seducing]] women.

